# NanoDrug Tools - Project Conventions

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 14+ (App Router) + TypeScript
- UI: shadcn/ui (Tailwind CSS v4)
- Backend: Supabase (Auth + PostgreSQL + Storage)
- Deployment: Vercel (frontend) + Supabase (backend services)
- Package manager: pnpm

## Directory Structure
- `src/app/` — Next.js App Router pages (route groups for organization)
- `src/components/ui/` — shadcn/ui components (DO NOT modify directly)
- `src/components/layout/` — Layout components (Navbar, Footer, etc.)
- `src/components/tools/` — Tool-specific components (each tool in its own file)
- `src/lib/supabase/` — Supabase client configuration (client.ts, server.ts, middleware.ts)
- `src/lib/calculations/` — Pure calculation logic (molecular weight, LNP formulas, etc.)
- `src/lib/utils.ts` — General utility functions
- `src/types/` — TypeScript type definitions

## Coding Conventions
- All components use TypeScript with strict types
- Separate calculation logic from UI components (put in `src/lib/calculations/`)
- Each online tool is an independent route under `src/app/tools/`
- Use Supabase server client (`src/lib/supabase/server.ts`) in Server Components
- Use Supabase browser client (`src/lib/supabase/client.ts`) in Client Components
- Protected routes (requiring auth): `/plasmid/*`, `/dashboard/*`
- Public routes: `/`, `/research/*`, `/tools/mol-weight`, `/tools/lnp-formula`

## Database (Supabase PostgreSQL)
- `profiles` — User profiles (extends auth.users)
- `plasmids` — Plasmid sequences (user-owned data with RLS)
- Always use Row Level Security (RLS) policies

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Use shadcn/ui components as building blocks
- Support dark/light mode via `next-themes`
- Responsive design: mobile-first approach
